  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient is a 61\u2011year\u2011old woman with a lifelong history of essential hypertension (since 1953) and progressive chronic kidney disease now at stage 3 (onset 1967). She has metabolic syndrome, obesity (BMI\u202f\u2265\u202f30), hyperlipidemia, and prediabetes treated with insulin, suggesting overt diabetes. Proteinuria and microalbuminuria due to type 2 diabetes indicate diabetic nephropathy. Anemia is present, likely anemia of chronic kidney disease. She also has knee osteoarthritis managed with naproxen, which is nephrotoxic in the setting of CKD. Socially, she reports limited social contact, chronic stress, full\u2011time employment, and a criminal record, which may affect adherence. No recent visits have been recorded since 1987, and many key laboratory values are missing.",
